<article class="env-corollary" id="05BK">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05BK">Corollary <span data-tag="05BK">4.8.4.16</span>.</a> Let $n \geq 0$ be an integer and let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an $n$-faithful functor of $\infty $-categories. Then, for every diagram $B \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{Fun}_{/\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}(B, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ is locally $(n-2)$-truncated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      It follows from Corollary <a data-tag="01BU" href="/tag/01BU">4.1.4.2</a> that $F$ induces an inner fibration $F': \operatorname{Fun}(B,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(B, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ and from Corollary <a data-tag="04Q6" href="/tag/04Q6">4.8.4.15</a> that $F'$ is $n$-faithful. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="05BD" href="/tag/05BD">4.8.3.36</a>, we deduce that every fiber of $F'$ is locally $(n-2)$-truncated. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
